{'symbol': 'PFE', 'date': '2022-09-07 06:45:00', 'title': "FDA GRANTS BREAKTHROUGH THERAPY DESIGNATION TO PFIZER'S GROUP B STREPTOCOCCUS VACCINE CANDIDATE TO HELP PREVENT INFECTION IN INFANTS VIA IMMUNIZATION OF PREGNANT WOMEN", 'text': 'NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PFIZER INC. (NYSE:PFE) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT ITS INVESTIGATIONAL GROUP B STREPTOCOCCUS (GBS) VACCINE CANDIDATE, GBS6 OR PF-06760805, RECEIVED BREAKTHROUGH THERAPY DESIGNATION FROM THE U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) FOR THE PREVENTION OF INVASIVE GBS DISEASE DUE TO THE VACCINE SEROTYPES IN NEWBORNS AND YOUNG INFANTS BY ACTIVE IMMUNIZATION OF THEIR MOTHERS DURING PREGNANCY. THE FDA DECISION IS INFORMED BY THE INTERIM ANALYSIS OF A PLACEBO-CONTROLLED PHASE 2 STUD'}